{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"8a392cc7-5aa9-4823-af08-c4ab603435bb","status":"SUCCESS","response":"The generator fix has been applied and documented in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-yeqkoo/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary of Changes\n\n1. **Fix in [`gen.py`](file:///tmp/h-yeqkoo/gen.py#L10-L14)**:\n   - Changed the lower bound property name in [`hr_target`](file:///tmp/h-yeqkoo/gen.py#L10) from `\"value\"` to `\"start\"`, producing `{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`.\n   - Using `\"start\"` instead of `\"value\"` instructs Intervals.icu to export an Instant-HR corridor rather than a zone-mapped Lap-HR target, preventing Garmin from clamping the targets to its local watch zones.\n\n2. **Documentation in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-yeqkoo/ANSWER.md)**:\n   - Detailed what was changed and why.\n   - Identified which parts of the colleague's notes applied (key name switch to `start` with `%lthr` units) and which parts were ignored (Intervals UI text grammar formatting and external API/sync reproduction steps).\n","duration_seconds":42.427252,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":187634,"output_tokens":1517,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":0,"total_tokens":189151}}}
